      "id": "45a779217609-q4",
      "number": 4,
      "question": "Who among the following was the chief guest of India's first Republic Day in 1950? &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; 1950 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2366;&#2352;&#2340; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2375; &#2327;&#2339;&#2340;&#2306;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2342;&#2367;&#2357;&#2360; &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2369;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351; &#2309;&#2340;&#2367;&#2341;&#2367; &#2341;&#2375;?",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Who among the following was the chief guest of India's first Republic Day in 1950?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; 1950 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2366;&#2352;&#2340; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2375; &#2327;&#2339;&#2340;&#2306;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2342;&#2367;&#2357;&#2360; &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2369;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351; &#2309;&#2340;&#2367;&#2341;&#2367; &#2341;&#2375;?</p></span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Rana Abdul Hamid &#2352;&#2366;&#2339;&#2366; &#2309;&#2348;&#2381;&#2342;&#2369;&#2354; &#2361;&#2366;&#2350;&#2367;&#2342;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Rana Abdul Hamid</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2366;&#2339;&#2366; &#2309;&#2348;&#2381;&#2342;&#2369;&#2354; &#2361;&#2366;&#2350;&#2367;&#2342;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Georgy Zhukov &#2332;&#2377;&#2352;&#2381;&#2332;&#2368; &#2333;&#2369;&#2325;&#2379;&#2357;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Georgy Zhukov</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2332;&#2377;&#2352;&#2381;&#2332;&#2368; &#2333;&#2369;&#2325;&#2379;&#2357;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Sukarno &#2360;&#2369;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2379;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Sukarno</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2369;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2379;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Queen Elizabeth &#2350;&#2361;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2319;&#2354;&#2367;&#2332;&#2366;&#2348;&#2375;&#2341;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Queen Elizabeth</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2350;&#2361;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2319;&#2354;&#2367;&#2332;&#2366;&#2348;&#2375;&#2341;</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<p>&#183; <b>Sukarno</b>, the first President of Indonesia, was the <b>chief guest at India's first Republic Day celebrations on 26 January 1950</b>. </p><p>&#183; This marked a significant diplomatic gesture, as both countries had recently gained independence (India in 1947, Indonesia in 1945) and were founding members of the Non-Aligned Movement.</p><p><b>Further insight:</b></p><p>&#183; <b>Rana Abdul Hamid</b>  -  A Pakistani military officer, irrelevant to the 1950 event.</p><p>&#183; <b>Georgy Zhukov</b>  -  Soviet Marshal; first Soviet chief guest in <b>1955</b>, not 1950.</p><p>&#183; <b>Queen Elizabeth</b>  -  First British monarch to attend R-Day in <b>1961</b> (as Queen of the UK and Commonwealth; India had already removed the British monarch as head of state by 1950).</p>",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "45a779217609-q5",
      "number": 5,
      "question": "When is the statehood day of Tripura observed? &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2346;&#2369;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2352;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2340;&#2381;&#2357; &#2342;&#2367;&#2357;&#2360; &#2325;&#2348; &#2350;&#2344;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>When is the statehood day of Tripura observed?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2346;&#2369;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2352;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2340;&#2381;&#2357; &#2342;&#2367;&#2357;&#2360; &#2325;&#2348; &#2350;&#2344;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "3 October 3 &#2309;&#2325;&#2381;&#2335;&#2370;&#2348;&#2352;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">3 October</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3 &#2309;&#2325;&#2381;&#2335;&#2370;&#2348;&#2352;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "12 March 12 &#2350;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2330;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">12 March</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">12 &#2350;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2330;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "21 January 21 &#2332;&#2344;&#2357;&#2352;&#2368;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">21 January</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">21 &#2332;&#2344;&#2357;&#2352;&#2368;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "21 February 21 &#2347;&#2352;&#2357;&#2352;&#2368;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">21 February</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">21 &#2347;&#2352;&#2357;&#2352;&#2368;</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<p>Statehood Day is celebrated every year as Manipur, Meghalaya, and Tripura on <b>January 21</b> as they attained statehood under the North Eastern Region (Reorganization) Act of 1971. Earlier before the north-eastern region was turned into seven sisters with the statehood of Manipur, Tripura, Meghalaya, Assam, Mizoram, Arunachal Pradesh, and Nagaland, the North Eastern composition consisted of Assam plains from the old Assam Province, the hill districts, and the North Eastern Frontier Tracts (NEFT) of the North-Eastern borderland.</p>",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "45a779217609-q6",
      "number": 6,
      "question": "In India, Teachers' Day is celebrated annually on September 5 to mark the birthday of: &#2349;&#2366;&#2352;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2358;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2325; &#2342;&#2367;&#2357;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; 5 &#2360;&#2367;&#2340;&#2306;&#2348;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2375; &#2332;&#2344;&#2381;&#2350;&#2342;&#2367;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2313;&#2346;&#2354;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2381;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2350;&#2344;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;:",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In India, Teachers' Day is celebrated annually on September 5 to mark the birthday of:</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2349;&#2366;&#2352;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2358;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2325; &#2342;&#2367;&#2357;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; 5 &#2360;&#2367;&#2340;&#2306;&#2348;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2375; &#2332;&#2344;&#2381;&#2350;&#2342;&#2367;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2313;&#2346;&#2354;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2381;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2350;&#2344;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;:</span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "APJ Abdul Kalam &#2319;.&#2346;&#2368;.&#2332;&#2375;. &#2309;&#2348;&#2381;&#2342;&#2369;&#2354; &#2325;&#2354;&#2366;&#2350;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">APJ Abdul Kalam</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2319;.&#2346;&#2368;.&#2332;&#2375;. &#2309;&#2348;&#2381;&#2342;&#2369;&#2354; &#2325;&#2354;&#2366;&#2350;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel &#2360;&#2352;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352; &#2357;&#2354;&#2381;&#2354;&#2349;&#2349;&#2366;&#2312; &#2346;&#2335;&#2375;&#2354;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2352;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352; &#2357;&#2354;&#2381;&#2354;&#2349;&#2349;&#2366;&#2312; &#2346;&#2335;&#2375;&#2354;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Sarvepalli Radhakrishnan &#2360;&#2352;&#2381;&#2357;&#2346;&#2354;&#2381;&#2354;&#2368; &#2352;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2325;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2339;&#2344;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Sarvepalli Radhakrishnan</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2352;&#2381;&#2357;&#2346;&#2354;&#2381;&#2354;&#2368; &#2352;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2325;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2339;&#2344;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Subhas Chandra Bose &#2360;&#2369;&#2349;&#2366;&#2359; &#2330;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352; &#2348;&#2379;&#2360;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Subhas Chandra Bose</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2369;&#2349;&#2366;&#2359; &#2330;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352; &#2348;&#2379;&#2360;</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<p>Teachers' Day is celebrated on September 5 in India to honor Dr. Sarvepalli Radhakrishnan, a great scholar, philosopher, and the second President of India.</p><p>&#183; When his students wanted to celebrate his birthday, he suggested that instead of celebrating his birthday, the day should be dedicated to teachers.</p><p>&#183; The first Teachers' Day was celebrated in 1962.</p><p>Other options:</p><p>&#183; APJ Abdul Kalam - Missile Man of India, his birthday (October 15) is celebrated as World Students' Day.</p><p>&#183; Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel - Iron Man of India, his birthday (October 31) is observed as National Unity Day.</p><p>&#183; Subhas Chandra Bose - Freedom fighter, his birthday (January 23) is observed as Parakram Diwas.</p><p>Hence, option (3) is the correct answer.</p>",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
