      "correctAnswer": "B",
      "solution": "<p>&bull; The birthday of Mahatma Gandhi is celebrated as the International Day of Non-Violence.</p><p>&bull; Mahatma Gandhi (Mohandas Karamchand Gandhi), born on October 2, 1869, in Porbandar, Gujarat, was a leader of India's freedom struggle against British rule, known as the \"Father of the Nation.\" </p><p>&bull; Advocating non-violence (Ahimsa) and truth (Satya), he led key movements like the Dandi Salt March (1930) and Quit India Movement (1942). </p><p>&bull; His philosophy of Satyagraha (non-violent resistance) inspired global civil rights movements. </p><p>&bull; Gandhi was assassinated on January 30, 1948, in New Delhi, leaving a legacy of peace, equality, and self-reliance.</p>",
